    "background_story": "In a lush, tropical forest, there lived a magnificent scarab beetle named Princess. She belonged to the Cetoniidae family, known for their striking colors and impressive size. Princess was a rare, gem-like beetle with a shimmering green carapace and delicate golden markings. She spent her days flitting from flower to flower, collecting nectar and pollen to sustain her colony. As the largest and most radiant of her kind, Princess was revered by the other insects in the forest. They would often gather around her, mesmerized by her beauty and strength. Despite her regal demeanor, Princess was a gentle soul, using her powerful mandibles to protect her friends from harm and defend her home from threats. Her legacy lived on, inspiring generations of Cetoniidae beetles to thrive in the vibrant forest ecosystem.",
